  "helpIntro": "The app opens on Matrix. Set your destination and pick a bus from the number table. The keypad is under … → Number entry, or swipe right from the left edge.",
  "helpBasics": "Basic operations",
  "helpResults": "Reading results",
  "helpRoutes": "Viewing routes",
  "helpTroubleshooting": "Troubleshooting",
  "helpTopTitle": "Matrix",
  "helpTopBody": "This is the screen that opens at launch. It shows destination, current location, distance, and the bus number table. To check a number on the keypad, open … → Number entry. You can also swipe right from the left edge. Return with … → Matrix, or swipe from the left edge again.",
  "helpDestinationTitle": "Set destination",
  "helpDestinationBody": "Tap the destination bar to open the map sheet. Search by name or long-press the map, or pick from History or Saved places. Switch between origin and destination at the top of the sheet.",
  "helpLocationTitle": "Location and origin",
  "helpLocationBody": "Location permission is requested at launch. Refresh with ↻ in the location bar, or choose an origin on the map with the map icon. Tap × to go back to your current location. While riding, distance is always measured from GPS.",
  "helpSavedPlacesTitle": "Saved places",
  "helpSavedPlacesBody": "Open Saved places in the destination sheet to register home and frequent places. Tap one to set it as your destination. Long-press the current destination to save it as-is.",
  "helpBusNumberTitle": "Enter bus number",
  "helpBusNumberBody": "Only when a number is missing from the table, open … → Number entry (or swipe from the left edge) and enter digits (e.g. 35). The app matches your trip and can still say board if that bus reaches a transfer stop.",
  "helpTableTitle": "Bus number table",
  "helpTableBody": "Bus numbers are grouped by direction and number of transfers. Tap to open the route map, long-press to board or alight. The bus you are riding turns orange.",
  "helpBoardTitle": "Start riding",
  "helpBoardBody": "On Number entry, the bus you enter is matched against routes to your destination. If a variant works, a yellow message like \"Get on if it's 35A!\" appears; tap Start riding to begin.",
  "helpSkipTitle": "Skip this bus!",
  "helpSkipBody": "When no matching variant runs toward your destination, you'll see red \"Skip this bus!\".",
  "helpDistanceTitle": "Distance colors",
  "helpDistanceBody": "When you are not riding, the badge is the straight-line distance to your destination. While riding, it is the distance to the current bus's alighting stop. Blue from 3 km, green from 1 km, yellow from 500 m, orange from 200 m, red under 200 m. Tap the badge while riding to open the route map. Long-press the badge to cancel navigation (this also clears the destination). If you start riding from the line map without a destination, the badge shows \"—\".",
  "helpRidingTitle": "Riding mode",
  "helpRidingBody": "Long-press a bus number to start riding. Long-press it again to alight for a transfer. While riding, arrival alerts ring by distance to your stop and tracking continues with the screen off. You are warned if the bus seems to be going the wrong way.",
  "helpLineMapTitle": "Line map",
  "helpLineMapBody": "… → Line map finds a route by bus number in the route data on your device and draws it on the map. Use the list button to browse saved routes. Long-press the number badge to board or alight (the last stop is the alighting stop).",
  "helpSettingsTitle": "Settings & alerts",
  "helpSettingsBody": "From … → Settings you can change language, keypad input, keypad sound and vibration, arrival alerts, and route data. Arrival alerts are distance-based to the alighting stop, with up to 3 thresholds — alarms play 1–3 times from furthest to closest. When the app is in the background, a notification is shown.",
  "helpPlanTitle": "Plan management",
  "helpPlanBody": "Open … → Plan to view your plan, upgrade to PREMIUM, or restore a previous purchase. FREE plan: up to {count} saved places and {count} history entries. PREMIUM: unlimited.",
  "helpNoRouteTitle": "No route found",
  "helpNoRouteBody": "Make sure you have downloaded route data in Settings and that your location and destination are in the same region. Route data is fetched around your current location.",
  "helpNetworkTitle": "Connection error",
  "helpNetworkBody": "Check Wi‑Fi or mobile data, then try again. Bus checks use the route data on your device, so they also work offline.",
